  "title": "Release notes: Remove WOWW notes to fix NEWS output",
  "description": "In `release-notes.adoc` the WOWW protocol notes were messed up:\n\n1. It consisted of two lines, messing up the output sorting algorithm for `NEWS` (https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/c9daa6b656ecf5032a6efc8f7e4f50ebb810d026/NEWS#L197-202)\n2. Lines weren't following the instructed “Full protocol name (Abbreviation)” syntax\n3. Lines had ending dots (which ended up in `NEWS` in the middle of the list)\n4. I don't know why it was in \"New Protocol Support\" section anyway if the existing dissector only had added/changed features, it was discussed already in https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/8356#note_1122847782 but got merged in anyway (and it doesn't sound like a thing for the Updated Protocol Support section)\n\nFeel free to suggest fixing `NEWS` output somehow else.",
